| `make_targets.gate_stop_grace_seconds` | integer | `15` | a whole number from 1 to 3600 (an hour) | `scripts/run_make_target.py`; `scripts/config_loader.py`; `scripts/resource_limits.py` (`tool_limits`, which refuses an `agents.tool_timeout_seconds` shorter than `make_targets.gate_timeout_seconds` plus twice `make_targets.gate_stop_grace_seconds` plus `agents.tool_gate_margin_seconds`, all of the same tree) | How long the gate runner waits after SIGTERM to make's session before it sends SIGKILL. Keep it longer than `e2e.server.stop_timeout_s`; the loader does not check this, and `tests/unit/scripts/test_run_make_target.py` fails a repository whose two values break it. The reason: a test stops its e2e server, which runs outside make's session, with SIGTERM and then SIGKILL after that wait, and a runner SIGKILL to pytest first leaves the server running. Raising it needs the same tree's `agents.tool_timeout_seconds` to stay at least `make_targets.gate_timeout_seconds` plus twice `make_targets.gate_stop_grace_seconds` plus `agents.tool_gate_margin_seconds`, or `tool_limits` refuses every agent tool of that tree with exit 14. Optional: absent, the loader's default applies and it writes `[using default] make_targets.gate_stop_grace_seconds = 15` to stderr. | the run's limit: `make_targets.gate_timeout_seconds` | always |
